/// ## What it does
/// Checks for files with overly permissive permissions.
///
/// ## Why is this bad?
/// Overly permissive file permissions may allow unintended access and
/// arbitrary code execution.
///
/// ## Example
/// ```python
/// import os
///
/// os.chmod("/etc/secrets.txt", 0o666)  # rw-rw-rw-
/// ```
